.SS "\fBC_ENUM\fP \fBaiReturn\fP aiGetMaterialTexture (const \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiMaterial\fP * mat, \fBC_ENUM\fP \fBaiTextureType\fP type, unsigned int index, \fBC_STRUCT\fP \fBaiString\fP * path, \fBC_ENUM\fP \fBaiTextureMapping\fP * mapping, unsigned int * uvindex, \fBai_real\fP * blend, \fBC_ENUM\fP \fBaiTextureOp\fP * op, \fBC_ENUM\fP \fBaiTextureMapMode\fP * mapmode, unsigned int * flags)"

.PP
Helper function to get all values pertaining to a particular texture slot from a material structure\&. This function is provided just for convenience\&. You could also read the texture by parsing all of its properties manually\&. This function bundles all of them in a huge function monster\&.
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fImat\fP Pointer to the input material\&. May not be NULL 
.br
\fItype\fP Specifies the texture stack to read from (e\&.g\&. diffuse, specular, height map \&.\&.\&.)\&. 
.br
\fIindex\fP Index of the texture\&. The function fails if the requested index is not available for this texture type\&. \fBaiGetMaterialTextureCount()\fP can be used to determine the number of textures in a particular texture stack\&. 
.br
\fIpath\fP Receives the output path If the texture is embedded, receives a '*' followed by the id of the texture (for the textures stored in the corresponding scene) which can be converted to an int using a function like atoi\&. This parameter must be non-null\&. 
.br
\fImapping\fP The texture mapping mode to be used\&. Pass NULL if you're not interested in this information\&. 
.br
\fIuvindex\fP For UV-mapped textures: receives the index of the UV source channel\&. Unmodified otherwise\&. Pass NULL if you're not interested in this information\&. 
.br
\fIblend\fP Receives the blend factor for the texture Pass NULL if you're not interested in this information\&. 
.br
\fIop\fP Receives the texture blend operation to be perform between this texture and the previous texture\&. Pass NULL if you're not interested in this information\&. 
.br
\fImapmode\fP Receives the mapping modes to be used for the texture\&. Pass NULL if you're not interested in this information\&. Otherwise, pass a pointer to an array of two aiTextureMapMode's (one for each axis, UV order)\&. 
.br
\fIflags\fP Receives the the texture flags\&. 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
AI_SUCCESS on success, otherwise something else\&. Have fun\&. 
.RE
.PP

